<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Sabe</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1894 CE (approx.) · capital Save</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Yoruba kingdom in central Benin, on the north-western edge of the Yoruba world, ruled by the Onisabe.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Known mainly from local tradition. Sabe, or Save, was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba-speakers</a> who traced their kings to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ife">Ile-Ife</a>, and took shape by the 16th century in the hilly country west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo</a> lands.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Onisabe ruled with town chiefs and religious societies. Sabe traded with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borgu">Borgu</a> and the coast, and was exposed to raids from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-dahomey">Kingdom of Dahomey</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bariba">Bariba</a> of Borgu. It was a small state that survived by shifting alliances.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Sabe came under French control after the conquest of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-dahomey">Dahomey</a> and was included in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-dahomey">French Dahomey</a> in 1894. The Onisabe remains a traditional ruler in the town of Save in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 CE – 1894 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:7.84%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE